.Dd October 25, 2026
.Dt ARCANA-CONSOLE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm arcana-console
.Nd the Arcana web console
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm service
.Cm arcana_console
.Cm start | stop | restart | status
.Pp
.Nm
.Op Fl dn
.Op Fl c Pa web.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The arcana console serves the web application and its JSON API over
HTTPS, with
.Xr libwebsockets 3 ;
it logs its users in
with WebAuthn, keeps the list of hosts, and talks to the
.Xr arcana-agent 8
of each host over cblink, with mutual TLS over TCP or through a local
socket.
It runs unprivileged; everything that changes a host is done by that
host's
.Xr arcana-agent 8 .
.Pp
It is three processes.
The supervisor, root when started by
.Xr rc 8 ,
listens on the addresses configured, keeps the pid file and starts the
worker again when it dies, logging how it ended; the worker serves on
the supervisor's sockets as the console's user, one at a time on one
loop, and runs what takes time (a call to a host) on task threads.
A worker that cannot start, its configuration or data being wrong,
stops the supervisor too.
Over HTTPS the worker never reads the key: the key manager, a process
it forks while still root, reads it, becomes the console's user, enters
capability mode
.Pq Xr capsicum 4
and signs what the worker's TLS handshakes need, digests sent on a
socket pair; a flaw that discloses the worker's memory discloses no
key.
Should the key manager end, the worker ends at its next handshake and
the supervisor starts both again.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Pa web.conf
The configuration; by default
.Ev ARCANA_WEB_CONF ,
or
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/web.conf .
.It Fl d
Become a daemon: the pid file is written, and the log goes to
.Xr syslog 3
instead of the standard error.
.It Fl n
No supervisor: the worker alone, for debugging.
.El
.Pp
The console shows, per host: its jails with their state and actions;
its rc.d services with their
.Xr rc.conf 5
variables; the routing table, nexthops, connections and sockets; the
packages that can be upgraded, on the host and in running jails; and
CPU, memory and ZFS usage.
Every call to a host is listed with a trace of what the host did.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Pa web.conf ,
in UCL, configures it.
Its
.Va server
block is the server's:
.Bl -tag -width "task_threads"
.It Va listen
A list of where to listen:
.Dq Ar address : Ns Ar port ,
.Dq Bq Ar address : Ns Ar port
for IPv6 (which then listens for IPv6 alone), or
.Dq unix: Ns Ar path .
By default 0.0.0.0:443 and [::]:443.
.It Va certfile , certkey
The certificate (with its chain) and key for HTTPS, RSA or EC; the key
is read by the key manager alone, as root.
TLS 1.2's key exchange is ECDHE alone (the key manager signs and
decrypts nothing), and TLS 1.0 and 1.1 are not spoken.
Over HTTPS the console speaks HTTP/2 to a client that offers it, as
browsers do, and HTTP/1.1 to one that does not; a WebSocket is carried
over HTTP/2 too (RFC 8441).
Without them the console speaks plain HTTP/1.1, for a proxy in front
of it or a local socket.
.It Va webroot
The web application; by default
.Pa /usr/local/www/arcana-console .
.It Va user
The user the worker runs as when started as root, by default
.Dq arcana ;
an empty one keeps the user it was started as.
.It Va task_threads
The task threads, by default 32: one per call to a host under way.
.It Va body_max
The largest request body, by default 8 MB.
.It Va pidfile
By default
.Pa /var/run/arcana-console.pid .
.El
.Pp
The rest is the console's:
.Bl -tag -width "update_check"
.It Va rp_id
The WebAuthn relying party: the console's host name as the browser sees
it, or a parent domain of it.
Keys are bound to the
.Va rp_id
they were registered under: after changing it, enrol again.
Required.
.It Va origin
The exact origin the browser uses, such as
.Ql https://console.example .
Opened at any other address, or without HTTPS other than on localhost,
the browser refuses security keys with a
.Dq SecurityError
.Pq Do The operation is insecure Dc in Firefox ;
the login screen then says which address the console is set up for.
Required.
.It Va rp_name
The name security keys show.
Default
.Ql Arcana .
.It Va datadir
Where the registered keys, the server list, the setup token and, without
.Va tls ,
the console's own certificate authority are kept; mode 0700, owned by
the worker's user.
Default
.Pa /var/db/arcana .
.It Va cookie_secure
Whether the session cookie is marked Secure.
Default true.
.It Va password_full
Whether a session opened by a password of the console's own has its
user's roles, as one opened by a security key does.
Default true.
False limits it as an API token's session: the console's settings,
sign-in, users, tokens, CA and host enrolment then take a key.
A session opened by a directory's (LDAP) password is limited so either
way.
.It Va tls
A block naming certificates for
.Xr arcana-agent 8
over TCP:
.Va ca ,
the authority that issued the hosts' certificates;
.Va cert
and
.Va key ,
the console's client certificate; and optionally
.Va ca_key ,
the authority's key, which lets the console enrol hosts.
Without the block the console makes an authority of its own in
.Va datadir
at first start and enrols hosts with it; see
.Xr arcana-enrol 8 .
.It Va update_check
False stops the console from asking the release feed for newer
versions.
Default true.
.It Va update_url
Another feed, in the shape of GitHub's
.Pa releases/latest .
.It Va agent_binary
The
.Xr arcana-agent 8
the console sends to hosts when asked to update them.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/sbin/arcana-agent ,
the one installed with the console.
.It Va agent_source
A git repository with the Arcana tree.
When set, a host can be asked to build
.Xr arcana-agent 8
from it; the console keeps what the host sends back in
.Pa agent/
under
.Va datadir
and sends that instead of
.Va agent_binary .
.It Va agent_ref
The branch or tag to build.
Default: the repository's own.
.It Va plugins_dir
The console plugins: extensions of the console's page, a directory
each, named by the plugin's id, with its
.Pa plugin.json
and the files it lists; not the hosts' plugins.
Read again when it changes, without a restart; a plugin is served once
an owner of the console enables it, to every signed-in user, and runs
with the page's rights.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/share/arcana-console/plugins ;
an empty one for none.
Which are enabled is kept in
.Pa console-plugins.json
in
.Va datadir .
.It Va android
A block naming an Android app that may log in:
.Va package ,
its package name, and
.Va fingerprints ,
the SHA-256 fingerprints of the certificates it is signed with, as
Android's
.Cm apksigner
or
.Cm keytool
print them, with or without colons; at most 8.
The console then serves
.Pa /.well-known/assetlinks.json
naming the app, which Android asks for before it lets the app use the
keys registered for
.Va rp_id ,
and takes WebAuthn ceremonies made in the app, whose origin is
.Ql android:apk-key-hash:\&
and the base64url of one of the fingerprints, as well as those of
.Va origin .
.Va rp_id
must be the host name the console is reached by for Android to find
the file.
Without the block,
.Pa /.well-known/assetlinks.json
is not found and only
.Va origin
is taken.
.It Ic cluster Brq Va self Va listen Va nodes
Consoles that are one, active on every node: each serves its browsers
and reads its own copy of the data directory's documents, and every
change is the cluster's.
The nodes elect a leader (Raft) over the arcana-cluster family on
.Va listen ,
a cblink URI
.Pq Li tcp://[::]:4311 ;
the leader numbers each change and answers once a majority of the
nodes holds it, and every node writes it in turn.
.Va nodes
names each node with its
.Va uri
and its
.Va origin ;
.Va self
is this one's name.
The first node named is the seed: its documents are the cluster's when
it starts, sent whole to a node that has none; the others' are replaced.
Three nodes, or five, keep a majority when one, or two, stop; a node
cut off from the majority reads, and refuses changes.
The workflow scheduler, the SD-WAN manager and mail run on the leader
alone.
Each node needs the CA of the first:
.Pa ca.pem
and
.Pa ca.key
copied to its
.Va datadir
before it starts; it makes its own certificate of that CA,
.Pa cluster/node.pem ,
which says
.Li urn:arcana:role:console
and its host's name, and the nodes take each other by it.
.Va rp_id
is a name every node's origin is under
.Pq Li console.example No for Li https://a.console.example ,
so that a security key registered on one signs in on every one.
.El
.Pp
The settings
.Va rp_name ,
.Va update_check ,
.Va update_url ,
.Va agent_binary ,
.Va agent_source
and
.Va agent_ref
can also be changed from the console, under Settings.
What is set there is kept in
.Pa settings.json
in
.Va datadir
and overrides
.Pa web.conf ;
a value put back to that of
.Pa web.conf
follows it again.
The others are read once, when the console starts, from
.Pa web.conf
alone.
.Pp
The worker checks every certificate it is configured with when it
starts, and refuses to start with the reason in the log.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "ARCANA_LWS_LOG"
.It Ev ARCANA_WEB_CONF
The configuration, when
.Fl c
does not name one.
.It Ev ARCANA_DEBUG
Set, the worker logs each connection or stream it ends itself, and
why: libwebsockets says nothing of those.
.It Ev ARCANA_LWS_LOG
What
.Xr libwebsockets 3
logs of its own, as its
.Dv LLL_
bits: 7 adds its warnings and notices to its errors, 15 information
too.
By default its errors alone.
In
.Xr rc.conf 5 :
.Va arcana_console_env Ns = Ns Qq ARCANA_LWS_LOG=7 .
.El
.Sh FIRST LOGIN
Until a security key is registered or a user has a password, the
console writes a one-time token to
.Pa setup-token
in
.Va datadir
and says so in its log.
The first registration in the browser needs it; later keys are added
from a logged-in session.
A key may be a hardware key or a passkey, such as a phone's.
.Pp
Where no key reaches the browser, a remote desktop's for one, the
console may be set up by a password instead: the same token, a user
name, and a password of 12 characters at least.
The user becomes an owner (the built-in
.Dq admin
when none is named) and is signed in; a key may be added later.
Once set up either way, the token is gone.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/web.conf
The configuration, with a sample next to it.
.It Pa /usr/local/sbin/arcana-console
The program.
.It Pa /usr/local/www/arcana-console
The web application.
.It Pa /var/db/arcana
.Pa credentials.json ,
.Pa servers.json ,
.Pa setup-token ,
and with the console's own authority
.Pa ca.pem ,
.Pa ca.key ,
.Pa console.pem ,
.Pa console.key .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/arcana_console
The
.Xr rc 8
script; variables
.Va arcana_console_enable ,
.Va arcana_console_web_conf
and
.Va arcana_console_pidfile .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libwebsockets 3 ,
.Xr arcana-agent 8 ,
.Xr arcana-enrol 8 ,
.Xr arcanactl 8 ,
.Xr jailconf 8
.Pp
The API is described in
.Pa docs/openapi.yaml
of the source tree.
